        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "899592ef-1199-5f27-9cc7-38367038fb64",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugène Ionesco, Paul Scott\n- Works: Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It, Oriflamme, The Raj Quartet, The Jewel in the Crown\n- Topics: French avant-garde theatre, British Raj, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Eugène Ionesco, born Eugen Ionescu on 26 November 1909 and died on 28 March 1994, was a Romanian-French playwright who wrote mostly in French and was a foremost figure of French avant-garde theatre.\n- Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It is a 1954 play by Eugène Ionesco that was based on his earlier short story Oriflamme.\n- The Raj Quartet is a series of novels published from 1965 to 1975 by British author Paul Scott.\n- Paul Scott, born on 25 March 1920 and died in March 1978, was an English novelist, playwright, and poet best known for The Raj Quartet.\n- The Jewel in the Crown is a 1984 British television serial about the final days of the British Raj in India during and after World War II, and it was based on Paul Scott's Raj Quartet novels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
